        "id": 3155470
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T08:27:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, wouldn\u0027t it be a bit inconsistent reading it there when the other looper logging properties are read in loop()? Also if it\u0027s read there, is there a way to force the property to be read the same way \"start \u0026\u0026 stop\" does for the ones set in loop().",
      "parentUuid": "669e447d_fcd3aa9b",
      "revId": "8a00e6123db232bc8aa1f38773594314b961b3b4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca81f850_14b1aa44",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Looper.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 319,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059977
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T17:18:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I understand the question or the requirement.\nLet me try to clarify my requirement.\n\nLooper init is hot code. I need to know that we\u0027re not adding any more work to it in the common path (where logging is not enabled). If we add more work, but only if logging is explicitly enabled, that\u0027s ok.\nIf you can modify your change to meet the above criteria then this will remove any performance-related objections that I have.\n\nDoes this make sense?\nThank you for working with us.",
      "parentUuid": "9d6290cc_7ae936b1",
      "revId": "8a00e6123db232bc8aa1f38773594314b961b3b4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "244292c6_efaff4cd",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Looper.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 319,
      "author": {
        "id": 1041495
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-12T08:23:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reading the verbose prop only on `setSlowLogThresholdMs` is not enough -- it won\u0027t work for threads that log because of `thresholdOverride`.\n\nReading the prop on both `setSlowLogThresholdMs` _and_ in loop() if thresholdOverride \u003e 0 might be enough to cover all the cases. This would require adding a new field to store the value (since it can no longer be kept on the stack as in the current patch).\n\nBut is Looper init really that hot? It\u0027s once per Looper thread, right?",
      "parentUuid": "ca81f850_14b1aa44",
      "revId": "8a00e6123db232bc8aa1f38773594314b961b3b4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5246ad7b_17b4812c",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Looper.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 319,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059977
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-12T18:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand why you\u0027d find my comment surprising! Let me try to rephrase.\nTo clarify, it\u0027s not hot in the sense that it gets called a lot, but it does get called in CUJs like app startup.\nI\u0027ve seen cases before where SysProp reads stall on SysProp flushes. I don\u0027t want to add the risk of such a stall to every app startup.\n\nI\u0027m happy with whatever solution you can come up with that doesn\u0027t read a sysprop unless the need for it was demonstrated by an explicit call to enable logging on this looper, and doesn\u0027t happen by default and during a CUJ.",
      "parentUuid": "244292c6_efaff4cd",
      "revId": "8a00e6123db232bc8aa1f38773594314b961b3b4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f4b26820_3e7e128d",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Looper.java",
