      },
      "lineNbr": 319,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003801
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-12T18:52:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yup, I wrote the original slow-looper-log code and my assumption was reading sysprops was _very_ fast. (I\u0027ve used sysprops in many places with for similar purposes)\n\nIf reading the sysprop is actually slow, then yeah we should avoid even doing it....\n\nBut I heard that the reason (or one of the reasons?) sysprop access got slow recently was because aconfig flags started using it a _lot_, but I believe they\u0027ve already moved away from sysprops.\n\nIs reading sysprops still a concern?\n\n(If it\u0027s really that slow, I\u0027m worried becase a lot of apps do Log.isLoggablle(), which I believe is just a wrapper around a sysprop read...)",
      "parentUuid": "5246ad7b_17b4812c",
      "revId": "8a00e6123db232bc8aa1f38773594314b961b3b4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
